// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_patchable_band_fire.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: rule 6 half 1 / claim E-A — the restore's carrying fire must be static
//          (spec §4.2; carried into check_band_pairing at parcel P1).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "must be static"
//
// THE SWEEP-5 K1 WITNESS. A textbook band — ON at line 50, its own restore at 100 — with
// the RESTORE'S fire handed to `patchable`. Every ownership check passes: the two records
// carry the same id, the same span, and the ON is above the restore. The band is
// well-formed; what is wrong is that its OFF edge can move.
//
// Past band_hi, Raster_BuildSchedule does not emit the record at all (engine/effects/
// raster.emp, .suppress) — so the ON op at line 50 still runs and the restore simply never
// does, and the tint runs to the bottom of the screen with nothing to turn it off. A
// moving-bottom band is spelled by moving the ON op instead, which keeps the OFF edge
// where the restore can always reach it. (That is the runtime half the ownership
// representation does NOT fix; it is design §4's SUP-1 and it belongs to parcel P3.)
//
// PARCEL-P1 NOTE. The band is now built by `band()` and split with an index, rather than
// hand-authored as an unowned cram/restore pair. That is not cosmetic: an unowned restore
// is refused for a different reason now (it carries no band id), so the old spelling would
// never have reached the guard this poison is for.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_two_restores.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_patchable_band_fire

const POISON_PBF_BAND = band(50, 100, stream_cram($48, [$0EEE, $0AAA, $0666]), 0)

const POISON_PATCHABLE_BAND_FIRE = [ POISON_PBF_BAND[0] ] ++ patchable([ POISON_PBF_BAND[1] ], ch: 0, lo: 100, hi: 150)

ensure(raster_program(POISON_PATCHABLE_BAND_FIRE).len > 0,
       "poison_patchable_band_fire: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
